y government the uk government  is going to breach international law now  brandon lewis told me on the program he  assured me several times that the  changes would not  break international law  what evidence do you have that it will  well can i can i well can i say to you  that brandon lewis is talking through  his hat and not for the first time  brandon lewis should know the tory  government  should know that where there are issues  to be resolved with the protocol  issues of smoothing out its application  there are mechanisms through which that  can happen there is a willingness there  is a willingness to engage by the  european commission but the british  government has refused to engage  has not been constructive has sought a  destructive path and is now proposing to  introduce legislation that will  undoubtedly breach international law and  by the way against the expressed  democratic wishes of people in the north  of ireland who went to the polls and who  made their democratic decision and have  returned a majority of members that  support the protocol all of the business  organizations across the north of  ireland will tell you that yes there are  issues that need to be resolved get that  done get that done by way of negotiation  but they will also tell you that the  protocol is necessary  that the protocol is working that the  protocol can work better because all of  them be very very clear no the jobs  prosperity and healthy economic growth  rely on access to the european market  nobody wants to jeopardize and forego  that and it's astonishing  that the british government brags  consistently that they will  change as they put it or ditch elements  of the protocol breach international law  bring themselves into a collision with  europe at a time when we have your uh  war in europe cause untold economic  damage to the north of ireland and why  why well because there is an internal  leadership problem within the tory party  it is disgraceful to use the north of  ireland to use ireland as a bargaining  chip  in their ongoing collision with europe  all designed to boost the ego at the  leadership ambitions of either boris  johnson or one of his would-be  successors it's dishonorable stuff  by any measure extraordinary stuff  that the british parliament it seems now  is set to have tabled before it  legislation specifically designed to  breach an international agreement that  that very parliament ratified  and an agreement that not so long ago  the current occupant of number 10  downing street just described as oven  ready and let me emphasize again uh in  the democratic test on these matters at  the people of the north have spoken  a majority of mlas elected to the  assembly support the protocol and when  there is a vote in 2024 assuming that  the assembly is up and running and even  if it's not a majority of those mlas  will vote to continue and support that  protocol  and in 2024 of course according to the  brexit deal politicians in northern  ireland specifically get to decide  whether or not they want to keep the  protocol in place it's effectively like  an exit clause that was worked into the  original deal  i just wonder how important you think it  is that those politicians in northern  ireland get to make the final decision  on the protocol because you know there  is  rumors uh that the  uh that the  bills tomorrow the legislation  introduced tomorrow could effectively  override that concept vote  well let me say this uh just remember  that when when brexit happened and the  vote was taken people in the north voted  to remain just just remember that  and people on on a cross community basis  from from all walks of life voted to  remain and i would wager if there was a  vote on the brexit question again next  week or next month that by an even  greater margin people in the north of  ireland would vote uh to remain so  brexit never had the democratic consent  or imprimatur of the people of the north  and therefore any idea that uh the tory  government would try to rob the elected  representatives of the north of ireland  of their rightful decision  on this matter would be absolutely  outrageous and and would mean that not  alone is the tory government uh  waging an onslaught against the protocol  prepared to breach international law and  walk away from its international  obligations but that in fact it is uh  damaging undermining power sharing in  the north of ireland and it would be  further and very very  very very dangerous evidence of a tory  attack on the good friday agreement uh  itself a very very dangerous suggestion  i mean i i should say at this point  obviously that brandon lewis says that  part of the reason they want to do this  is to effectively restore all elements  of the good friday uh agreement as the  uh assemblies  listen sophie sophie  sophia that just needs to be scotched  i mean that that's just that's frankly  beyond disingenuous  uh the tory government consistently uh  abuses language uh in in a way that is  mesmerizing they say they want to  protect the good friday agreement when  they take the very actions that  undermine and that could potentially  destroy the good friday agreement that's  the reality and they are doing this in  plain sight they're colluding with the  section of political unionism to keep  the executive down in belfast to ensure  that the north-south element of the good  friday agreement is now  not operating to wage an attack on the  protocol the protocol to guarantee  access to the european market but  crucially to ensure no hardening of the  border on on ireland they have acted  unilaterally  in terms of legislation to deal with  victims and survivors of the conflict  they threatened still to withdraw from  the european convention and human rights  all of the building blocks in other  words upon which the good friday  agreement has been carefully constructed  by all of us are now being openly  attacked and undermined by the tory  g